      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Focusing on specific visual cues is often a tactic used to profile, but in high-density areas, officers should look for patterns of behavior rather than just appearance. Certain groups might exhibit a high degree of territoriality or display specific, coordinated movements that suggest pre-planned activity. Pay attention to how individuals interact with their environment—are they avoiding eye contact, or are they aggressively asserting space? These non-verbal cues, combined with the context of the location, are more reliable indicators than clothing alone.",
